{"id":"c41922bd3c1b1d0f3c27c62e4af3e67d8f458023","axis":"silent","repo":"strapi/strapi","sha":"c41922bd3c1b1d0f3c27c62e4af3e67d8f458023","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/docs/packages/core/content-type-builder/index.md","lines":["@@ -50,6 +50,8 @@ The `content-structure` service writes the folder groups that the admin navigati"," "," The admin part registers a menu link and the plugin API `forms`, which other plugins use to add fields and validation to the CTB modals. `DataManagerProvider` keeps the working copy of the schema in a Redux slice with undo and redo (`undoRedo.ts`). Modals in `components/FormModal` edit attributes and types. The read permission is `plugin::content-type-builder.read`, which `bootstrap` registers."," ","+`GET /content-type-builder/schema` returns `settings` next to the schemas: the `renameMigrations` plugin setting, and `strictRelations`, which is `true` only when `api.documents.strictRelations` is the literal `true` (the document service rejects other non-boolean values). The document service enforces `required` on relations and media only under that flag. When `strictRelations` is `false`, the advanced form of relation attributes disables the **Required** checkbox, with a hint and a tooltip explaining the flag. Media attributes, single or multiple, keep an editable checkbox because the Content Manager already requires them on publish. A `required: true` already in the schema stays checked, and the save keeps it.","+"," ## Related"," "," - [Schema sync](../../../architecture/07-schema-sync.md): what happens to the tables after CTB writes a file."],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/docs/packages/core/core/configuration/01-security-defaults.md","lines":["@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@ module.exports = {"," - Enforced only on **published** (non-draft) writes — drafts stay lenient so you can save work in progress with associations still missing."," - Applies to required media and relations, including those nested inside components and dynamic zones."," - On by default in newly scaffolded apps only; existing projects keep the legacy (lenient) behaviour until they opt in, so enabling it will start rejecting previously-accepted writes that omit a required association.","+- While the flag is off, the Content-Type Builder disables the **Required** checkbox of relation attributes and explains how to turn enforcement on. Media stays editable because the Content Manager already requires it on publish. A `required: true` already in the schema stays checked and is kept on save."," "," ## Content API authentication (refresh tokens)"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/core/content-manager/admin/src/utils/tests/validationMedia.test.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@","+import { createYupSchema } from '../validation';","+","+const gallery = {","+  gallery: { type: 'media' as const, multiple: true, required: true },","+};","+","+describe('createYupSchema required multiple media', () => {","+  test('rejects an empty array on publish', async () => {","+    const schema = createYupSchema(gallery, {}, { status: 'published' });","+","+    await expect(schema.validate({ gallery: [] })).rejects.toThrow();","+  });","+","+  test('rejects null and a missing value on publish', async () => {","+    const schema = createYupSchema(gallery, {}, { status: 'published' });","+","+    await expect(schema.validate({ gallery: null })).rejects.toThrow();","+    await expect(schema.validate({})).rejects.toThrow();","+  });","+","+  test('accepts a selected file on publish', async () => {","+    const schema = createYupSchema(gallery, {}, { status: 'published' });","+","+    await expect(schema.validate({ gallery: [{ id: 1 }] })).resolves.toEqual({","+      gallery: [{ id: 1 }],","+    });","+  });","+","+  test('accepts an empty array on a draft', async () => {","+    const schema = createYupSchema(gallery, {}, { status: 'draft' });","+","+    await expect(schema.validate({ gallery: [] })).resolves.toEqual({ gallery: [] });","+  });","+","+  test('accepts an empty array when the field is not required', async () => {","+    const schema = createYupSchema(","+      { gallery: { type: 'media', multiple: true, required: false } },","+      {},","+      { status: 'published' }","+    );","+","+    await expect(schema.validate({ gallery: [] })).resolves.toEqual({ gallery: [] });","+  });","+","+  test('still accepts a file on required single media', async () => {","+    const schema = createYupSchema(","+      { cover: { type: 'media', multiple: false, required: true } },","+      {},","+      { status: 'published' }","+    );","+","+    await expect(schema.validate({ cover: { id: 1 } })).resolves.toEqual({ cover: { id: 1 } });","+    await expect(schema.validate({ cover: null })).rejects.toThrow();","+  });","+});"],"additions":55,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/core/content-manager/admin/src/utils/validation.ts","lines":["@@ -149,6 +149,27 @@ const createYupSchema = (","                   )","                 ).test(arrayValidator(attribute, options)),","               };","+            case 'media':","+              return {","+                ...acc,","+                // mixed().required() rejects null and undefined. An untouched multiple","+                // field is loaded as [], which would still publish.","+                [name]: transformSchema(","+                  attribute.multiple","+                    ? yup.mixed().test({","+                        name: 'media-required',","+                        message: translatedErrors.required,","+                        test(value: unknown) {","+                          if (options.status === 'draft' || !attribute.required) {","+                            return true;","+                          }","+","+                          return !Array.isArray(value) || value.length > 0;","+                        },","+                      })","+                    : yup.mixed()","+       